{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20392",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.06,
      "end_seconds": 3.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Good afternoon, how are you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 5.79,
      "end_seconds": 10.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "morning, uh, doctor, sorry about the rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.61,
      "end_seconds": 14.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Is this your first time with this clinic?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.1,
      "end_seconds": 22.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "mm, first time with this one, yes. A friend recommended it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.88,
      "end_seconds": 27.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.2,
      "end_seconds": 34.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Um, so... chest tightness. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.88,
      "end_seconds": 39.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.62,
      "end_seconds": 44.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Right, I've had it for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.9,
      "end_seconds": 47.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Have you noticed any triggers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.46,
      "end_seconds": 55.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Uh, pollen season definitely sets it off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.59,
      "end_seconds": 62.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 64.31,
      "end_seconds": 73.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.28,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get itchy eyes as well. There's wheezing when I exercise as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.19,
      "end_seconds": 77.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "alright, is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 78.98,
      "end_seconds": 81.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "It's, It's every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.27,
      "end_seconds": 86.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "has there been sneezing a lot too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.19,
      "end_seconds": 105.4,
      "duration_seconds": 18.21,
      "text": "Yeah, that that too. As for itchy eyes, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. As for itchy eyes, a eight out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.86,
      "end_seconds": 113.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.3,
      "end_seconds": 128.59,
      "duration_seconds": 14.29,
      "text": "Hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema. I'm, I'm on Asthalin inhaler, when needed. Actually, I take cetirizine, 10 milligrams, maybe, when it flares."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.68,
      "end_seconds": 132.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.92,
      "end_seconds": 139.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Well, not with me. I'll bring it it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.34,
      "end_seconds": 156.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.75,
      "end_seconds": 159.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Amoxicillin, I'd say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.76,
      "end_seconds": 163.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.4,
      "end_seconds": 174.89,
      "duration_seconds": 10.49,
      "text": "I do a yoga class on Thursdays. I look after my grandchildren most days. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.43,
      "end_seconds": 178.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.98,
      "end_seconds": 184.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Actually, just a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.88,
      "end_seconds": 188.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.44,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.09,
      "end_seconds": 195.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "My uncle has high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.46,
      "end_seconds": 200.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.37,
      "end_seconds": 205.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I have eczema, for five years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.01,
      "end_seconds": 207.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Right, right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.39,
      "end_seconds": 212.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.88,
      "text": "ah, I've had asthma, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.85,
      "end_seconds": 219.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Any chest pain, fever or coughing up phlegm?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.32,
      "end_seconds": 225.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Ah, uh, none of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.44,
      "end_seconds": 229.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Any ankle swelling or blue lips?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 230.17,
      "end_seconds": 234.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "No, um, none that I've noticed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.34,
      "end_seconds": 237.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.63,
      "end_seconds": 241.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.79,
      "end_seconds": 246.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.62,
      "end_seconds": 250.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 252.1,
      "end_seconds": 263.23,
      "duration_seconds": 11.13,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Saturation 98 percent, respiratory rate 16. Temperature is 36.8 degrees, pulse is 68 beats a minute, blood pressure 122 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.99,
      "end_seconds": 266.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.4,
      "end_seconds": 273.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.72,
      "end_seconds": 285.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.55,
      "end_seconds": 290.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.96,
      "end_seconds": 309.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "I can hear a faint wheeze at the end of breathing out, otherwise the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 310.67,
      "end_seconds": 313.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Yeah, um, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.42,
      "end_seconds": 327.28,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "You can relax now. Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy. I'd also keep reflux in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.69,
      "end_seconds": 333.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Actually, will it clear up?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.24,
      "end_seconds": 346.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.46,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's exercise-triggered asthma with seasonal allergy, and we'll know more once the an allergy test is back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.23,
      "end_seconds": 384.03,
      "duration_seconds": 27.8,
      "text": "Let's get an allergy test, for seasonal symptoms. Let's book a peak flow diary to look into asthma. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. What I'm giving you is budesonide-formoterol inhaler, 200 micrograms, one puff twice a day, long term. That's for asthma control. Rinse your mouth after the preventer inhaler and use the spacer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 384.87,
      "end_seconds": 411.44,
      "duration_seconds": 26.57,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Keep an eye out, and if the inhaler isn't helping or you cannot speak in full sentences, call us the same day or go to emergency. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 413.04,
      "end_seconds": 416.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "Thank you, um, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.8,
      "end_seconds": 419.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "see you soon"
    }
  ]
}